# Platform Abstraction Rules

## About Platform Abstraction

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/platform/platform-abstraction.md`.

## Hard Rule

`#[cfg(target_os = ...)]` and `#[cfg(target_arch = ...)]` live only inside
`crates/flequit-platform/src/platform/`. If an OS check is needed elsewhere,
the abstraction is missing — add it to `flequit-platform` instead.

## Capability Gating

Unsupported features are reported through `Capability`, not runtime errors.
Query before calling; hide the UI affordance when unavailable.

`SystemTray`, `GlobalHotkey`, `MultiWindow`, `OsTrash`, `ArbitraryFilePath` are
desktop-only. `LocalNotification` and `FilePicker` exist everywhere.

## Paths

Use `paths::data_dir()` / `config_dir()` / `cache_dir()` / `log_dir()`.
Mobile keeps everything inside the app sandbox.

## File Handles

Mobile file pickers return URIs / security-scoped handles, not paths.
Return a `FileHandle` abstraction and read/write through it.

## Lifecycle

Never write save-on-exit logic. Mobile OSes kill the process without warning.
Persist on every operation. Handle `Suspend` / `Resume` / `LowMemory` explicitly.
